===Etymology===
{{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|échelon}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|eschelon||rung of a ladder}}.Compared with {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|échelle||ladder}},from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|eschiele||ladder}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|scāla||ladder,stairs}},from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*skand-}}, also {{m|ine-pro|*skend-}} (“to leap,climb”).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈɛʃəlɒn/|lang=en}}, {{IPA|/ˈɛkəlɒn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[level]] or [[rank]] in an organization, profession, or society.
# {{lb|en|military}} A [[formation]] of troops, ships, etc. in [[diagonal]] [[parallel]] [[row]]s.
# {{lb|en|cycling}} A line of [[rider]]s seeking maximum [[drafting]] in a [[crosswind]], resulting in a diagonal line across the road.

